<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <dimen name="text_margin">16dp</dimen>

    <!--
      How far a control that floats over the map sits from the edge of what it floats over, on every sample
      screen that places one itself — and the samples' own cards floating over a map with it, so the two line up.

      It lives in the examples rather than the SDK because nothing in the SDK arranges a floating control: the
      screen picks the corner and supplies the spacing, so there is nothing on that side for this number to
      agree with. It is a convention among the hosts, and this is where the hosts keep it.

      A `dimen` rather than a Kotlin constant because it has to be readable from XML layouts, which is where
      most of its uses are; Compose reads it with `dimensionResource`.

      `fragment_vps_local_history_map.xml` keeps a literal `8dp` on purpose — that screen's bottom edge is its
      own `traceInfo` TextView. Do not "correct" it to this.
    -->
    <dimen name="overlay_inset">16dp</dimen>
</resources>
